          %p
            When applied to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            then this mechanism produces not just
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/force"} force
            fields but also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermionic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matter"} matter
            in the resulting
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Yang-Mills-Dirac+theory"} Einstein-Yang-Mills-Dirac theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#KKReductionOf11dSupergravity"} KK-reduction of 11d Supergravity
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometrodynamics"} geometrodynamics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamics"} dynamical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            geometry in the form of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            with all matter and other forces being special incarnations of this.
          %p
            Since in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+relativity"} general relativity
            also the size and shape of the fiber
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is dynamical, generically
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theories"} effective field theories
            arising from KK-compactification contain spurious fields parameterizing the geometry of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dilaton"} dilaton
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume"} volume
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli"} moduli
            fields. Since these moduli fields are not observed in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenologically
            unviable. However, in variants of gravity such as higher dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            there are possibilities for the moduli to obtain masses and hence for the KK-models to become viable after all. This is the problem of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stabilization"} moduli stabilization
